=== P3 Dashboard widget 0003 AnomalyDetectorWidget (Android) ===
Web source : web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/AnomalyDetectorWidget.tsx
Native out : apps/android/app/src/main/java/io/teslasync/android/dashboardwidgets/AnomalyDetectorWidget.kt
Unit test  : apps/android/app/src/test/java/io/teslasync/android/dashboardwidgets/AnomalyDetectorWidgetTest.kt
UI test    : apps/android/app/src/androidTest/java/io/teslasync/android/dashboardwidgets/AnomalyDetectorWidgetUiTest.kt

CAPABILITY (available): Jetpack Compose + Material 3 + Kotlin (compose BoM, kotlin-android,
kotlin-compose plugins), JDK 21 runtime, minSdk=26 targetSdk=36 compileSdk=36. Build runs.

DOCUMENTED DEVIATIONS (honesty covenant #9 - no silent drift):
1. Path: the prompt path `com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/` is a template artifact - Kotlin package
   identifiers cannot contain a hyphen and the real module namespace is `io.teslasync.android`
   (app/build.gradle.kts). Shipped at the idiomatic, detekt-clean package
   `io.teslasync.android.dashboardwidgets` so it integrates with `io.teslasync.android.components.*`
   and the shared `io.teslasync.shared.core.*` S8 state holders.
2. Gradle module: the prompt gate uses `:app:`; the real module path is `:android:`
   (settings.gradle.kts maps :android -> app/). Gate run below uses `:android:`.
3. Telemetry: web "view.opened" -> the sanctioned typed taxonomy
   TelemetryEvent.ScreenView(screen="AnomalyDetectorWidget", platform="android", appVersion)
   (ADR-016 forbids raw/free-form event strings; ScreenView is the screen-open event).
4. Severity labels: per-widget `widget.anomalyDetector.severity.*` keys are absent from the
   generated P1/S10 catalog; reused the coherent localized triplet
   translation_quietHours_severity_{critical,warn,info} (web uses a raw-severity fallback).
   Title/activeCount/noAnomalies map 1:1 to translation_widget_anomalyDetector_*. Relative time
   reuses translation_freshness_{justNow,minutes,hours,days}.
5. Tests: adapter + per-state + a11y-label unit tests in src/test (JVM, run by the gate below);
   per-state render + semantics in src/androidTest (instrumented, runs under A9-0002 connectedCheck
   on a device). The androidTest sources are type-checked here via compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin.
   check-placeholders is re-pointed from the template path to the real source paths.
6. WidgetShell is NOT a listed dependency and has no Android equivalent yet -> self-contained chrome.

PREREQUISITE: the generated API clients io.teslasync.shared.core.api.generated.* are .gitignored
(.gitignore: apps/**/generated/). Ran `npx tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts`
(10 Kotlin + 10 C# files) before building the shared :core + :android app.

